  "id": "COMPOUND:18720 - PROTEIN:5673",
  "verbalization": "Artochamin F appears to have a direct target relationship with Leukocyte antigen CD37, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Parameritannin A-1 and Cyanidin 3-(6''-succinyl-glucoside). These compounds are all linked to LS174T through a series of molecular interactions, suggesting a potential pathway where Artochamin F may influence the activity of Leukocyte antigen CD37, which then modulates the function of LS174T. The shared targeting of Leukocyte antigen CD37 by different compounds implies a possible role in the regulation of LS174T, possibly through a common mechanism involving the interaction with these targets. The evidence suggests that Artochamin F may act as a modulator of the biological process that involves Leukocyte antigen CD37 and its downstream effect on LS174T, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
